silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_05_profunctor_generalization_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProfunctorGeneralizationConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_05_profunctor_generalization_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'ProfunctorGeneralizationConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, HeteroLegProfunctor_D_Mittens: the heterogeneous profunctor that sends each pair (TaxonomyCategory_source, D_Mittens_object) to a set of typed arrows; e.g., (ITIS_category, D_Mittens_classification) -> the set of typing arrows from ITIS taxon rows to classification nodes; enables FelisCatusTSN183798 from a separate ITIS category to be a profunctorial source for the classification leg; also, WeightedColimit_Mittens: MittensColimitApex expressed as the W-weighted colimit of D_Mittens; where W = the hom-profunctor restricted to the twelve source objects; this is the most general statement of the Mittens colimit construction." .
